    <briefdescription>
<para>ConcurrentHashTable - is a resizeable concurrent hashtable. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The number of resizings limited up to x2^31. This hashtable is useful to have efficient access to aggregate <ref refid="_static_data_splitter_8cpp_1ad2fefd8832b4b1ea3dbb1f621063bbff" kindref="member">data(like strings,
type descriptors...)</ref> and to keep only single copy of such an aggregate. The hashtable allows only concurrent insertions:</para>
<para>KeyDataTy* = insert ( const KeyTy&amp; );</para>
<para>Data structure:</para>
<para>Inserted value KeyTy is mapped to 64-bit hash value -&gt; <verbatim>     [------- 64-bit Hash value --------]
     [  StartEntryIndex ][ Bucket Index ]
               |                |
         points to the     points to
         first probe       the bucket.
         position inside
         bucket entries
</verbatim></para>
<para>After initialization, all buckets have an initial size. During insertions, buckets might be extended to contain more entries. Each bucket can be independently resized and rehashed(no need to lock the whole table). Different buckets may have different sizes. If the single bucket is full then the bucket is resized.</para>
<para>BucketsArray keeps all buckets. Each bucket keeps an array of Entries (pointers to KeyDataTy) and another array of entries hashes:</para>
<para>BucketsArray[BucketIdx].Hashes[EntryIdx]: BucketsArray[BucketIdx].Entries[EntryIdx]:</para>
<para>[Bucket 0].Hashes -&gt; [<ref refid="classuint32__t" kindref="compound">uint32_t</ref>][<ref refid="classuint32__t" kindref="compound">uint32_t</ref>] [Bucket 0].Entries -&gt; [KeyDataTy*][KeyDataTy*]</para>
<para>[Bucket 1].Hashes -&gt; [<ref refid="classuint32__t" kindref="compound">uint32_t</ref>][<ref refid="classuint32__t" kindref="compound">uint32_t</ref>][<ref refid="classuint32__t" kindref="compound">uint32_t</ref>][<ref refid="classuint32__t" kindref="compound">uint32_t</ref>] [Bucket 1].Entries -&gt; [KeyDataTy*][KeyDataTy*][KeyDataTy*][KeyDataTy*] ......................... [Bucket N].Hashes -&gt; [<ref refid="classuint32__t" kindref="compound">uint32_t</ref>][<ref refid="classuint32__t" kindref="compound">uint32_t</ref>][<ref refid="classuint32__t" kindref="compound">uint32_t</ref>] [Bucket N].Entries -&gt; [KeyDataTy*][KeyDataTy*][KeyDataTy*]</para>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_concurrent_hash_table_by_ptr" kindref="compound">ConcurrentHashTableByPtr</ref> uses an external thread-safe allocator to allocate KeyDataTy items. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
